## Lakehouse view-only materialization

Context: the Lakehouse backend always copied the mapped triples out of the
R2RML gateway view into a `…_data` Delta table (CTAS + `OPTIMIZE`). That copy
costs storage, costs build time proportional to graph size, and goes stale
between builds. A new per-domain **Materialization** option lets a Lakehouse
domain make `…_data` a pass-through view over the gateway instead, so nothing
is duplicated and every read sees live source data. Inferred triples keep
their own Delta table — they have no source to be derived from — and Graph
Analytics materializes a disposable snapshot for the duration of a run, since
its iterative BFS would otherwise re-run the whole mapping query on every
pass. Lakebase and Neo4j domains are unaffected: the resolver forces `table`
for any backend other than `databricks`, because their own graph is not what
the analytics job reads.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py`
   Added the `LAKEHOUSE_MATERIALIZATIONS` vocabulary, `normalize_lakehouse_materialization`, and `resolve_lakehouse_materialization` — the single resolver, which returns `table` for any non-Lakehouse backend.
2. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py`
   Added `build_data_view_sql` / `create_data_view` for the pass-through view, `drop_relation`, and `apply_data_relation` as the one entry point both pipelines use. Each branch cross-drops the relation of the other kind first, since Databricks refuses to replace a TABLE with a VIEW or the reverse.
3. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline.py`
   Resolves the mode in `__init__`, routes through `apply_data_relation`, skips `OPTIMIZE` in view mode, and reports `build_mode` / `materialization` in the task result and build-run record.
4. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/_build_pipeline.py`
   Same routing for the shared pipeline used by every engine, with progress wording that matches the mode.
5. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/_table_naming.py`
   Added the `…_analytics` suffix and `analytics_snapshot_fqn` for the disposable analytics snapshot.
6. `src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobMetrics.py`
   Added the `analytics_snapshot` context manager: a no-op for a materialized domain, a CTAS + guaranteed drop for a view-only one. Raises when no snapshot can be prepared rather than letting the job scan the view.
7. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DigitalTwin.py`
   Wrapped `compute_graph_metrics` in `analytics_snapshot` — the single hook both the interactive endpoint and the scheduler pass through.
8. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/objects.py`
   `_drop_sort_key` now orders `_graph` → `_data` → gateway among views, so a view-mode `_data` drops before the gateway it reads from; `object_base` groups a leftover `…_analytics` with its domain for purging.
9. `src/back/core/graphdb/delta/health.py`, `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   Both status payloads expose `materialization`.
10. `src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py`, `src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py`
    Persist and normalize `lakehouse_materialization` across `get_domain_info`, `save_domain_info`, `get_domain_template_data`, the empty-domain defaults, and the export/import round-trip.
11. `src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html`, `src/front/static/domain/js/domain-information.js`, `src/front/static/domain/js/domain.js`, `src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js`
    Added the Materialization selector, shown only for the Lakehouse backend, with both save paths sending the field and resetting it to `table` when the backend is not Lakehouse.
12. `src/front/static/config/js/settings.js`, `src/front/static/query/js/query-databricks-build.js`, `src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_databricks_build.html`
    The Lakehouse health card and the Build page now label `…_data` as a view when it is one, and note that the triple count is a live query.
13. `tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_package.py`, `tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_triple_store_backend_config.py`, `tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_materialize.py`, `tests/units/core/test_job_metrics.py`, `tests/units/domain/test_domain_service.py`, `tests/units/domain/test_domain_session.py`, `tests/units/settings/test_delta_objects.py`
