## Fix: Analytics showed KPIs and charts for a deleted Knowledge Graph

Context: after dropping every Unity Catalog object of a domain (tables, views),
opening Knowledge Graph → Analytics showed the "No Knowledge Graph has been
built yet" banner *and*, at the same time, populated KPI tiles, distribution
tiles and a ranking chart. The page asserted two contradictory things at once.

Root cause: the banner and the charts were driven by two independent sources
that were never connected.

- The banner comes from a live check in `_loadEntityTypes` — first
  `__TRIPLESTORE_CONFIG.graph_name`, then `/dtwin/sync/stats`. With the objects
  dropped, `store.get_aggregate_stats()` raises, the endpoint returns an
  `InfrastructureError`, `data.success` is falsy, and the banner is shown.
- The charts come from `analyticsResume()` → `analyticsLoadLatest()` →
  `/dtwin/metrics/latest`, which is a pure registry read of the last persisted
  run. It is *correctly* unaware of whether the graph objects still exist — it
  also has to serve history — but it survives the graph being deleted.

`analyticsResume()` called `analyticsLoadLatest()` unconditionally, so the live
"there is no graph" signal only ever painted a banner and disabled the Run
button. It never gated the rendering. Fixed in the presentation layer, where the
live signal already is, rather than by making a cheap registry read probe the
warehouse on every call.

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/query/js/query-analytics.js`
   Added module-level `_graphMissing`, set on both no-graph exit paths of
   `_loadEntityTypes` (empty `graph_name`, failed stats probe) and cleared on
   the success path so a rebuild brings the dashboard back.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-analytics.js`
   New `_clearAnalyticsResults()` — the exact inverse of `_renderAnalyticsData`:
   hides `#analyticsResults`, the scope subtitle and the provenance line, hides
   Interpret/Audit, nulls `_analyticsData`, and destroys the Chart.js instances
   (a hidden container still redraws on resize).
3. `src/front/static/query/js/query-analytics.js`
   `analyticsResume()` now clears and returns when `_graphMissing`, before the
   fetch — checking after would still flash the stale charts. Nulling
   `_analyticsData` also stops Interpret from posting a dropped graph's metrics
   to the LLM.
4. `src/front/static/query/js/query-analytics.js`
   The no-graph banner now says previous results are no longer shown because the
   graph they describe does not exist, and points at KG → Management → Runs,
   which retains the history. An empty dashboard with no explanation reads as a
   broken page to someone who saw charts there before.
5. `tests/units/front/test_analytics_stale_result_gate.py` (new, 11 tests)
   The contract: the live signal is recorded on every path, the dashboard is
   gated before the fetch, the clear helper hides the container and drops the
   cached payload, and the banner explains the disappearance.

Verification: drove the real module in Node with a stubbed DOM and a `fetch`
that fails `/dtwin/sync/stats` while `/dtwin/metrics/latest` still returns a
result — the deleted-objects situation. Before the guard the Nodes/Edges tiles
filled with `4,321` / `9,876` from the stale run and Interpret was revealed,
reproducing the report; after it they stay empty and Interpret stays hidden. Ran
the same harness with a healthy `/dtwin/sync/stats` to confirm a live graph
still renders its stored result and Run stays enabled.

