## MCP: expose class bridges with target-domain description so the agent can switch domains

Context: MCP sessions bind to a single domain via `select_domain`. Class
bridges were exposed only as `{target_domain, target_class_name, target_class_uri, label}`
with no description of the target and no filter on MCP-visible domains, and
the only cross-domain path (`get_entity_context(follow_bridges=True)`) is a
read-only peek that never switches the selected domain. An interrogating LLM
had no signal to hop into another domain, and no way to know whether a hop
would even be reachable. This change surfaces the target-domain description
alongside every bridge, filters bridges to MCP-visible targets on the
external surface (keeping every authored bridge on the internal UI path), and
reframes the tool prompts around `select_domain(<target>)` as the primary
hop, with `follow_bridges` documented as a peek only. Ships under v0.8.0,
tracked by Asana task 1217792873648378 and SPEC
`.planning/mcp-bridge-context/SPEC.md`.

Changes:

1. `src/back/objects/digitaltwin/NodeContextService.py`
   Added `enrich_bridge_targets(bridges, *, session_mgr, settings,
   registry_*, drop_unavailable=True)` and the private
   `_load_mcp_target_descriptions` helper. Resolves `target_domain`
   descriptions once from `RegistryService.list_mcp_domains()`, drops
   non-visible targets by default (external / MCP contract), or keeps every
   bridge when `drop_unavailable=False` (internal UI). Registry errors
   soft-fail so a broken registry never breaks a node-context response.
   Wired the enricher into `_resolve_bridges`, so `follow_bridges=true` skips
   non-visible targets before any BFS SQL scan.
2. `src/api/routers/domains.py`
   `GET /api/v1/domain/classes` runs each class's bridges through
   `NodeContextService.enrich_bridge_targets(...)` before serialisation.
3. `src/api/routers/digitaltwin.py`
   Added `target_domain_description: str = ""` to the `NodeContextBridge`
   Pydantic response model so the enriched field survives serialisation
   through `NodeContextResponse`.
4. `src/api/routers/internal/dtwin.py`
   `GET /dtwin/classes` now depends on `Settings` and calls
   `enrich_bridge_targets(..., drop_unavailable=False)` on top of
   `class_bridge_entries` so the ontology-authoring UI keeps seeing every
   bridge, enriched with the target-domain description when available.
5. `src/mcp-server/server/app.py`
   `_format_class_context_block` and `_format_node_context_response` now
   render `Target domain: <description>` under each bridge, and replace the
   legacy `get_entity_context(follow_bridges=True)` hint with a
   `select_domain(<target_domain>)` hop-then-query workflow.
   `FastMCP.instructions` gains a "CROSS-DOMAIN BRIDGES" paragraph that
   spells out the switch workflow and clarifies that `follow_bridges` is a
   peek only. `get_entity_context` docstring mirrors the same guidance.
6. `documentation/mcp.md`
   `describe_entity` sample output now shows the enriched `[Context]` bridge
   block, and a new "Hopping across domains" subsection describes the
   `describe_entity → select_domain(target) → describe_entity/GraphQL`
   workflow, the peek-vs-hop distinction, and the MCP-visibility filter.
   `documentation/sphinx/guides/mcp.md` inherits via `{include}`.
7. `.planning/mcp-bridge-context/SPEC.md` (new)
   AI-feature-gate SPEC per `.cursor/12-ai-feature-lifecycle.mdc`: bridge
   payload contract, tool-surface delta, success criteria, four eval
   dimensions (`bridge_description_present`, `unavailable_bridge_omitted`,
   `hop_tool_selection`, `no_silent_peek`), and failure modes.
8. `tests/eval/datasets/mcp/bridge_switch.jsonl` (new, 10 examples)
   Material-change floor per the AI-feature gate: happy hops, hidden targets,
   peek-vs-switch, ambiguous multi-target choice, registry soft-fail.
9. `tests/units/api/test_domain_classes_endpoint.py` (+3 tests)
   Bridges enriched with target description when visible; bridges dropped
   when target is not MCP-visible; soft-fail keeps bridges unchanged when
   the registry lookup returns `None`.
10. `tests/units/api/test_node_context_endpoint.py` (+3 tests)
    Same coverage on `/api/v1/digitaltwin/nodes/context`, plus a
    `follow_bridges=true` check that no BFS SQL scan runs against a filtered
    target.
11. `tests/units/api/test_dtwin_nodes_context.py` (+2 tests)
    Internal `/dtwin/classes` route keeps every bridge (UI authoring path)
    while still enriching descriptions when the target is MCP-visible.
12. `tests/units/mcp/test_node_context_formatting.py` (+3 tests)
    Formatter guards: bridge target description renders, blank description
    is omitted, the `select_domain(<target_domain>)` hint replaces the old
    `follow_bridges=True` peek hint on both `[Context]` and
    `Cross-domain Bridges:` blocks.

